Reason: the draw loop visited every tile of the room every frame and the renderer threw most of them away as
off-screen: in rm_a3h04 about 4,660 of 4,787 tiles a frame, about 0.75 µs each on the real Wii (~3.5 ms a frame),
which kept the sand shaft over its frame budget. A renderer can now report the rectangle outside which drawTile would
draw nothing (new optional hook tilesVisibleRect). Each run of same-depth tiles gets a grid of the tiles' boxes, built
when the tile-order version (now also moved by tile_set_scale) or the room changes; a run of the draw list then visits
only the tiles in the cells under that rectangle (shifted by the layer's offset, with a margin), in their order, and
draws each exactly as before, and a hidden layer is passed over as before. Tiles whose box isn't finite are always
visited. The tile drawing code moved into drawRoomTile, shared by both paths.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

